4. Examination Result and Grace-Mark Validation

1. Problem Statement
Process marks in multiple subjects, check subject-wise pass criteria, apply a limited grace-mark policy,
and generate a final result without exceeding maximum marks.

2. Objectives
•	Check each subject against the pass mark.
•	Use grace marks only within the stated limit.
•	Calculate total, percentage, and final status.

3. Assumptions
•	Marks are out of 100 and the pass mark is 40 per subject.
•	At most 3 grace marks may be added to one subject that is short by no more than 3 marks.
•	Final marks cannot exceed 100.

4. Algorithm
1. Store subject marks in a dictionary.
2. For each subject, if marks are 37–39, add enough grace marks to reach 40, within the 3-mark limit.
3. Check whether all subjects pass.
4. Calculate total and percentage and display the result.

